        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cfbb6263-4aad-55aa-aa21-655c4f40d614",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michelle Dockery, Dan Stevens, Colin Wratten\n- Works: The Turn of the Screw (2009 film), Downton Abbey, The Musketeers, Inside Men, Waking the Dead, EastEnders\n- Roles: Ann, Dr Fisher, Lady Mary Crawley\n- Organizations: BBC, ITV, PBS\n\nFacts:\n- In the 2009 BBC television film The Turn of the Screw, the story is told in flashbacks during consultations between the institutionalised Ann, played by Michelle Dockery, and Dr Fisher, played by Dan Stevens.\n- From 2010 to 2015, Michelle Dockery was widely known for playing Lady Mary Crawley in the ITV and PBS period drama series Downton Abbey.\n- For Downton Abbey, Michelle Dockery received three consecutive Emmy Award nominations for Outstanding Lead Actress in a Drama Series and a Golden Globe Award nomination.\n- Colin Wratten produced the BBC television film The Turn of the Screw.\n- Colin Wratten also produced episodes of the BBC dramas The Musketeers, Inside Men, and Waking the Dead, as well as episodes of the BBC soap EastEnders.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
